.TH CCOL_EVENT_LOOP_REG_COUNT 3 "2026-07-12" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_event_loop_reg_count \- number of currently-registered ccol_event_reg handles
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

size_t ccol_event_loop_reg_count(ccol_event_loop loop);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function returns the number of live registrations. A live
registration is a ccol_event_loop_add() call that nothing has removed
yet. It is not the number of entries in the epoll interest list. One
fd with both directions registered counts as 2. Two independent
ccol_event_reg handles back that fd, and they share one entry.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
loop  ccol_event_loop to query.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns the count of the registrations on success.
Returns (size_t)-1 when loop is CCOL_EVENT_LOOP_INVALID, or a handle
that is stale or that something already destroyed.
.fi
.SH THREAD SAFETY
.nf
Safe to call at the same time as ccol_event_loop_add(), as
ccol_event_loop_remove(), and as a dispatch on any reactor thread. It
returns a snapshot that is consistent. That snapshot is a single
atomic load, and it cannot tear. No lock protects the value.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_event_loop_add (3),
.BR ccol_event_loop_remove (3)
